Partitioning is a technique used to divide a large database table into smaller logical parts called partitions. In this practical, we used range partitioning based on customer ID. Customers with IDs below 104 are stored in partition p1, IDs from 104 to 106 are stored in p2, and IDs 107 onwards are stored in p3. We performed insert, update and delete operations and retrieved records from each partition separately. Partitioning improves query performance, data management and handling of large tables.

